## 1. Project Overview & Architecture

### What is Nyaya?
* **Type:** A rule-based Natural Language Processing (NLP) chatbot built in Python.
* **Core Tech:** Regular Expressions (Regex) pattern matching and Flask-based responsive Web UI.
* **Domain:** Indian Legal System (Constitutional Law, Criminal Procedure, IPC Sections, Consumer Rights, Cyber Law, and more).
* **Context:** NLP Course Project, Christ University, Bangalore.

### System Architecture Flow

The chatbot follows a pipeline-based architecture, transforming raw user inputs into legal responses:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[User Input] --> B{Language Mode?}
    B -- English --> C[preprocess.py]
    B -- Tamil --> D[preprocess_tamil.py]
    C --> E[matcher.py]
    D --> F[matcher_tamil.py]
    E --> G[intent.py Lookup]
    F --> H[intent_tamil.py Lookup]
    G --> I{Pattern Matches?}
    H --> J{Pattern Matches?}
    I -- Yes --> K[Select Random Intent Response]
    I -- No --> L[Select Random Fallback Response]
    J -- Yes --> M[Select Random Intent Response]
    J -- No --> N[Select Random Fallback Response]
    K --> O[Output to Console / Web UI]
    L --> O
    M --> O
    N --> O
```

