## 2. Deep Dive: Core Logic & Code Breakdown

### A. Preprocessing (`preprocess.py` & `preprocess_tamil.py`)
Before running regex matches, the chatbot normalizes the raw user query. This step prevents punctuation or capitalization differences from breaking the pattern matching.

```python
# preprocess.py (English)
def preprocess(text: str) -> str:
    text = text.lower().strip()
    text = re.sub(r'\s+', ' ', text)
    # keep dots so abbreviations like 'i.p.c' or 'sec.' stay intact
    text = re.sub(r"[^\w\s\.]", ' ', text)
    return text
```

```python
# preprocess_tamil.py (Tamil)
def preprocess(text: str) -> str:
    text = text.strip()
    text = re.sub(r'\s+', ' ', text)
    # Remove punctuation but preserve Tamil Unicode characters, digits, dots, and spaces
    text = re.sub(r"[^\u0B80-\u0BFF\w\s\.]", ' ', text)
    return text
```

> [!NOTE]
> **Tamil Unicode Range:** The regex range `\u0B80-\u0BFF` specifically matches the Tamil block in Unicode. This ensures that Tamil letters are not stripped away by the punctuation filter.

